<title>USA: Atlas reacquires Grassy Mountain.</title>
<headline>Atlas reacquires Grassy Mountain.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlas Corp said Newmont Gold Co has agreed to reconvey the Grassy Mountain gold property in Malheur County, Oregon, back to Atlas.</p>
<p>The company said it paid Newmont $206,000, issued a $500,000 unsecured, non-interest bearing promissory note due September 18, 1997, and assumed bonding requirements for exploration reclamation of $146,000.</p>
<p>Atlas originally acquired the property in 1986. In 1992, it leased the Grassy Mountain and Musgrove Creek properties from Atlas for total payments of $30 million.</p>
<p>Musgrove Creek -- in Lemhi County, Idaho -- was reconveyed to Atlas in February, it noted.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
